IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `aia-core`
IMPORT `aia-timeline`
IMPORT `P8-gate`

-- P8-art77: Article 77, powers of authorities protecting fundamental rights and cooperation with market surveillance authorities. LAYER 1.
-- Group General (from 2 August 2026). The Omnibus REPLACED the title and paragraph 1 and INSERTED paragraphs 1a and 1b (`▼M1`); paragraphs 2 to 4 are as enacted (`▼B`).
-- Paragraph 1 is encoded in both versions, each in its own function; through the dispatcher the as-enacted branch is dead, because the group applies from 2 August 2026
-- and the amended text from 27 July 2026. The as-enacted functions are tested directly.
-- The consolidated text is a rendering with no legal effect.

DECLARE `Art 77 act` IS ONE OF
    `Art 77(1) as enacted inform the market surveillance authority of the Member State concerned of the request`
    `Art 77(1a) grant the relevant public authority or body access to the information or documentation`
    `Art 77(1b) cooperate closely and provide each other with the mutual assistance necessary to fulfil their respective mandates`
    `Art 77(2) identify the public authorities or bodies referred to in paragraph 1 and make a list of them publicly available`
    `Art 77(2) notify the list to the Commission and to the other Member States`
    `Art 77(2) keep the list up to date`
    `Art 77(3) make a reasoned request to the market surveillance authority to organise testing of the high-risk AI system through technical means`
    `Art 77(3) organise the testing with the close involvement of the requesting public authority or body within a reasonable time`
    `Art 77(4) treat the information or documentation obtained in accordance with the confidentiality obligations set out in Article 78`

§ `Article 77(1): the power to request and access documentation, both versions`

-- VERSION as enacted: "National public authorities or bodies which supervise or enforce the respect of obligations under Union law protecting fundamental rights, including the right to
-- non-discrimination, in relation to the use of high-risk AI systems referred to in Annex III shall have the power to request and access any documentation created or maintained under this Regulation ... when access to that documentation is necessary".
-- src:eu-ai-act-2024-1689:1789 | 1. National public authorities or bodies which supervise or enforce the respect of obligations under Union law protecting fundamental rights, including the right to non-discrimination, in relation to the use of high-risk AI systems referred to in Annex III shall have the power to request and access any documentation created or maintained under this Regulation in accessible language and format when access to that documentation is necessary for effectively fulfilling their mandates within the limits of their jurisdiction. The relevant public authority or body shall inform the market surveillance authority of the Member State concerned of any such request.
@ref Art 77(1) as enacted, first sentence (src:eu-ai-act-2024-1689:1789)
GIVEN `the authority or body supervises or enforces the respect of obligations under Union law protecting fundamental rights` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the supervision or enforcement is in relation to the use of high-risk AI systems referred to in Annex III` IS A BOOLEAN
      `access to the documentation is necessary for effectively fulfilling the mandate of the authority or body within the limits of its jurisdiction` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 77(1) as enacted the national public authority or body has the power to request and access any documentation created or maintained under this Regulation` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the authority or body supervises or enforces the respect of obligations under Union law protecting fundamental rights` AND `the supervision or enforcement is in relation to the use of high-risk AI systems referred to in Annex III`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the power is for authorities that supervise or enforce the respect of obligations under Union law protecting fundamental rights "in relation to the use of high-risk AI systems referred to in Annex III", with no "only" (ruling (c))
    ELSE IF `access to the documentation is necessary for effectively fulfilling the mandate of the authority or body within the limits of its jurisdiction`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall have the power to request and access ... when access to that documentation is necessary for effectively fulfilling their mandates within the limits of their jurisdiction" (a power gated by "when": split site (ii), fork F-77-1-when)

-- src:eu-ai-act-2024-1689:1789 | 1. National public authorities or bodies which supervise or enforce the respect of obligations under Union law protecting fundamental rights, including the right to non-discrimination, in relation to the use of high-risk AI systems referred to in Annex III shall have the power to request and access any documentation created or maintained under this Regulation in accessible language and format when access to that documentation is necessary for effectively fulfilling their mandates within the limits of their jurisdiction. The relevant public authority or body shall inform the market surveillance authority of the Member State concerned of any such request.
@ref Art 77(1) as enacted, second sentence (src:eu-ai-act-2024-1689:1789)
GIVEN `the authority or body has made a request for documentation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 77(1) as enacted second sentence the authority or body must inform the market surveillance authority of the Member State concerned of the request` MEANS
    IF `the authority or body has made a request for documentation`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the sentence is about "any such request"

-- src:eu-ai-act-2024-1689:1789 | 1. National public authorities or bodies which supervise or enforce the respect of obligations under Union law protecting fundamental rights, including the right to non-discrimination, in relation to the use of high-risk AI systems referred to in Annex III shall have the power to request and access any documentation created or maintained under this Regulation in accessible language and format when access to that documentation is necessary for effectively fulfilling their mandates within the limits of their jurisdiction. The relevant public authority or body shall inform the market surveillance authority of the Member State concerned of any such request.
@ref Art 77(1) as enacted, second sentence (src:eu-ai-act-2024-1689:1789)
GIVEN `the authority or body has made a request for documentation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Arts 72 to 79 party` `Art 77 act`
`Art 77(1) as enacted the authority's duty to inform the market surveillance authority of the request` MEANS
    IF NOT `the authority or body has made a request for documentation`
    THEN FULFILLED  -- nothing is owed: no request has been made
    ELSE
        PARTY `Arts 72 to 79 party national public authority protecting fundamental rights`
        MUST `Art 77(1) as enacted inform the market surveillance authority of the Member State concerned of the request`
        HENCE FULFILLED

-- VERSION as amended: "... shall have the power to request and access any information or documentation created or maintained from the relevant market surveillance authority pursuant to
-- this Regulation in accessible language and machine-readable format by electronic means where access to that information or documentation is necessary ...".
-- src:1274 | 1. National public authorities or bodies which supervise or enforce the respect of obligations under Union law protecting fundamental rights, including the right to non-discrimination, shall have the power to request and access any information or documentation created or maintained from the relevant market surveillance authority pursuant to this Regulation in accessible language and machine-readable format by electronic means where access to that information or documentation is necessary for effectively fulfilling their mandates within the limits of their jurisdiction. This Article is without prejudice to the competences, tasks, powers and independence of the relevant national public authorities or bodies under their mandates.
@ref Art 77(1) as amended, first sentence (src:1274)
GIVEN `the authority or body supervises or enforces the respect of obligations under Union law protecting fundamental rights` IS A BOOLEAN
      `access to the information or documentation is necessary for effectively fulfilling the mandate of the authority or body within the limits of its jurisdiction` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 77(1) as amended the national public authority or body has the power to request and access any information or documentation created or maintained from the relevant market surveillance authority pursuant to this Regulation` MEANS
    IF NOT `the authority or body supervises or enforces the respect of obligations under Union law protecting fundamental rights`
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the power is for "National public authorities or bodies which supervise or enforce the respect of obligations under Union law protecting fundamental rights", with no "only" (ruling (c))
    ELSE IF `access to the information or documentation is necessary for effectively fulfilling the mandate of the authority or body within the limits of its jurisdiction`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall have the power to request and access ... where access to that information or documentation is necessary for effectively fulfilling their mandates within the limits of their jurisdiction" (a power gated by "where": split site (ii), fork F-77-1-when)

-- The dispatcher: the group's gate, then the version in force. The as-enacted facts and the amended facts are both asked; the as-enacted branch is dead (NOTES.md).
-- src:1274 | 1. National public authorities or bodies which supervise or enforce the respect of obligations under Union law protecting fundamental rights, including the right to non-discrimination, shall have the power to request and access any information or documentation created or maintained from the relevant market surveillance authority pursuant to this Regulation in accessible language and machine-readable format by electronic means where access to that information or documentation is necessary for effectively fulfilling their mandates within the limits of their jurisdiction. This Article is without prejudice to the competences, tasks, powers and independence of the relevant national public authorities or bodies under their mandates.
@ref Art 77(1), both versions (src:1274)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the authority or body supervises or enforces the respect of obligations under Union law protecting fundamental rights` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the supervision or enforcement is in relation to the use of high-risk AI systems referred to in Annex III` IS A BOOLEAN
      `access to the information or documentation is necessary for effectively fulfilling the mandate of the authority or body within the limits of its jurisdiction` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 77(1) the national public authority or body has the power to request and access the information or documentation` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Arts 72 to 79 the group General applies on the date asked` `the date asked`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the group General applies from the date Art 113 gives
    ELSE CONSIDER `Omnibus Art 4 the version in force` `the date asked`
         WHEN `as enacted` THEN `Art 77(1) as enacted the national public authority or body has the power to request and access any documentation created or maintained under this Regulation` `the authority or body supervises or enforces the respect of obligations under Union law protecting fundamental rights` `the supervision or enforcement is in relation to the use of high-risk AI systems referred to in Annex III` `access to the information or documentation is necessary for effectively fulfilling the mandate of the authority or body within the limits of its jurisdiction`  -- VERSION as enacted
         WHEN `as amended` THEN `Art 77(1) as amended the national public authority or body has the power to request and access any information or documentation created or maintained from the relevant market surveillance authority pursuant to this Regulation` `the authority or body supervises or enforces the respect of obligations under Union law protecting fundamental rights` `access to the information or documentation is necessary for effectively fulfilling the mandate of the authority or body within the limits of its jurisdiction`  -- VERSION as amended

-- src:1274 | 1. National public authorities or bodies which supervise or enforce the respect of obligations under Union law protecting fundamental rights, including the right to non-discrimination, shall have the power to request and access any information or documentation created or maintained from the relevant market surveillance authority pursuant to this Regulation in accessible language and machine-readable format by electronic means where access to that information or documentation is necessary for effectively fulfilling their mandates within the limits of their jurisdiction. This Article is without prejudice to the competences, tasks, powers and independence of the relevant national public authorities or bodies under their mandates.
@ref Art 77(1) as amended, second sentence (src:1274)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 77(1) as amended second sentence this Article is without prejudice to the competences, tasks, powers and independence of the relevant national public authorities or bodies under their mandates` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Arts 72 to 79 the group General applies on the date asked` `the date asked`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the group General applies from the date Art 113 gives
    ELSE JUST TRUE  -- one answer: "This Article is without prejudice to the competences, tasks, powers and independence of the relevant national public authorities or bodies under their mandates"

§ `Article 77(1a) and (1b): access and cooperation (inserted by the Omnibus)`

-- src:1276 | 1a. Subject to the conditions specified in this Article, the market surveillance authority shall grant the relevant public authority or body referred to in paragraph 1 access to such information or documentation, including by requesting such information or documentation from the provider or the deployer, where necessary and without undue delay.
@ref Art 77(1a) (src:1276)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the conditions specified in this Article are met` IS A BOOLEAN
      `access to the information or documentation is necessary` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 77(1a) the market surveillance authority must grant the relevant public authority or body access to the information or documentation` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Arts 72 to 79 the group General applies on the date asked` `the date asked`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the group General applies from the date Art 113 gives
    ELSE IF `the conditions specified in this Article are met` AND `access to the information or documentation is necessary`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subject to the conditions specified in this Article, the market surveillance authority shall grant the relevant public authority or body ... access ..., where necessary and without undue delay" (an unmet "where" gate counts as the text's no: ruling (b)) (fork F-77-1a-duty)

-- src:1276 | 1a. Subject to the conditions specified in this Article, the market surveillance authority shall grant the relevant public authority or body referred to in paragraph 1 access to such information or documentation, including by requesting such information or documentation from the provider or the deployer, where necessary and without undue delay.
@ref Art 77(1a) (src:1276)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the conditions specified in this Article are met` IS A BOOLEAN
      `access to the information or documentation is necessary` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Arts 72 to 79 party` `Art 77 act`
`Art 77(1a) the market surveillance authority's duty to grant access to the information or documentation` MEANS
    IF (NOT (`Arts 72 to 79 the group General applies on the date asked` `the date asked`)) OR (NOT `the conditions specified in this Article are met`) OR (NOT `access to the information or documentation is necessary`)
    THEN FULFILLED  -- nothing is owed: the group General does not apply on the date asked, or the conditions of the duty are not met
    ELSE
        PARTY `Arts 72 to 79 party market surveillance authority`
        MUST `Art 77(1a) grant the relevant public authority or body access to the information or documentation`
        HENCE FULFILLED

-- src:1277 | 1b. Market surveillance authorities and public authorities or bodies referred to in paragraph 1 shall cooperate closely and provide each other with the mutual assistance necessary to fulfil their respective mandates, with a view to ensuring the coherent application of this Regulation and Union law protecting fundamental rights and streamlining procedures, while respecting their respective competences, tasks, powers and independence. This shall include, in particular, exchange of information where necessary for the effective supervision or enforcement of this Regulation and the respective other Union legislation.
@ref Art 77(1b) first sentence (src:1277)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 77(1b) first sentence the market surveillance authorities and the public authorities or bodies must cooperate closely and provide each other with the mutual assistance necessary to fulfil their respective mandates` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Arts 72 to 79 the group General applies on the date asked` `the date asked`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the group General applies from the date Art 113 gives
    ELSE JUST TRUE  -- one answer: "Market surveillance authorities and public authorities or bodies referred to in paragraph 1 shall cooperate closely and provide each other with the mutual assistance necessary"

