§ `Article 77(2): the list of authorities`

-- "By 2 November 2024": the text's own date is earlier than the date the group applies (2 August 2026), so the date is a constant and the gated function answers NOTHING before the group applies (fork F-dated-before-application).
-- src:1279 | 2. By 2 November 2024, each Member State shall identify the public authorities or bodies referred to in paragraph 1 and make a list of them publicly available. Member States shall notify the list to the Commission and to the other Member States, and shall keep the list up to date.
@ref Art 77(2) first sentence (src:1279)
`Art 77(2) first sentence the date by which each Member State must identify the authorities and make the list publicly available` MEANS Date 2 11 2024

-- src:1279 | 2. By 2 November 2024, each Member State shall identify the public authorities or bodies referred to in paragraph 1 and make a list of them publicly available. Member States shall notify the list to the Commission and to the other Member States, and shall keep the list up to date.
@ref Art 77(2) first sentence (src:1279)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`Art 77(2) the date by which each Member State must identify the authorities and make the list publicly available on the date asked` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Arts 72 to 79 the group General applies on the date asked` `the date asked`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the group General applies from the date Art 113 gives (the text's own date, 2 November 2024, is earlier)
    ELSE JUST `Art 77(2) first sentence the date by which each Member State must identify the authorities and make the list publicly available`

-- src:1279 | 2. By 2 November 2024, each Member State shall identify the public authorities or bodies referred to in paragraph 1 and make a list of them publicly available. Member States shall notify the list to the Commission and to the other Member States, and shall keep the list up to date.
@ref Art 77(2) first sentence (src:1279)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Arts 72 to 79 party` `Art 77 act`
`Art 77(2) first sentence the Member State's duty to identify the authorities and make the list publicly available` MEANS
    CONSIDER `Art 77(2) the date by which each Member State must identify the authorities and make the list publicly available on the date asked` `the date asked`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FULFILLED  -- nothing is owed on the date asked: the group General does not yet apply
    WHEN JUST `the deadline` THEN
        PARTY `Arts 72 to 79 party Member State`
        MUST `Art 77(2) identify the public authorities or bodies referred to in paragraph 1 and make a list of them publicly available`
        WITHIN (Day `the deadline`) MINUS (Day `Art 113 the Regulation enters into force`)
        HENCE FULFILLED
        LEST BREACH BY `Arts 72 to 79 party Member State` BECAUSE "the authorities were not identified and the list was not made publicly available by 2 November 2024"

-- src:1279 | 2. By 2 November 2024, each Member State shall identify the public authorities or bodies referred to in paragraph 1 and make a list of them publicly available. Member States shall notify the list to the Commission and to the other Member States, and shall keep the list up to date.
@ref Art 77(2) second sentence (src:1279)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 77(2) second sentence the Member States must notify the list to the Commission and to the other Member States and keep the list up to date` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Arts 72 to 79 the group General applies on the date asked` `the date asked`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the group General applies from the date Art 113 gives
    ELSE JUST TRUE  -- one answer: "Member States shall notify the list to the Commission and to the other Member States, and shall keep the list up to date"

-- src:1279 | 2. By 2 November 2024, each Member State shall identify the public authorities or bodies referred to in paragraph 1 and make a list of them publicly available. Member States shall notify the list to the Commission and to the other Member States, and shall keep the list up to date.
@ref Art 77(2) second sentence (src:1279)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Arts 72 to 79 party` `Art 77 act`
`Art 77(2) second sentence the Member State's duty to notify the list` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Arts 72 to 79 the group General applies on the date asked` `the date asked`)
    THEN FULFILLED  -- nothing is owed: the group General does not apply on the date asked
    ELSE
        PARTY `Arts 72 to 79 party Member State`
        MUST `Art 77(2) notify the list to the Commission and to the other Member States`
